(q)
"Lands under Irrigable Command" means such lands as are irrigated or capable of being irrigated by flow or lift from an
irrigation work being under its command and shall include also such cultivated land which received in the opinion of the
Executive Engineer, by seepage or otherwise from an irrigation work or by indirect flow, percolation or drainage from or
through adjoining land, an advantage beneficial to the crop;
(r)
"Lift Irrigation" means irrigation by lifting water by means of a pump operated otherwise than by human or animal power;
